  secret: true env fields can carry a plaintext default.

  Nothing prevents an entry from declaring an env field as secret: true
  while also setting a non-empty default. Since commonEntry marshals the
  whole decoded struct into Entry.Payload, that default is persisted
  verbatim and returned by Browse/Detail — i.e. a "secret" field's default
  value would be openly exposed through catalog reads.





